   "type": "status",
   "url": "https://x.com/heymakio/status/2022753794891878460",
   "id": "2022753794891878460",
   "text": "Proposed protocol: Shared Public Cache for Social Data (X, Instagram, Facebook, etc.)\n\nToday, if 1,000 developers fetch the same public post, the platform is queried 1,000 times, whether through the official API or third-party tools (eg. Apify).\n\nWhat if the first successful fetch populated a shared cache layer?\n\nSubsequent requests for that same public data could be served from the cache instead of triggering another upstream call.\n\nIn theory, this coordination layer alone could reduce data access costs by 10x+.",
